All tests in the `llm` package pass.

**Cause:** In `llm/llama_server.go`, `shouldDisableMMProjOffload` unconditionally disabled GPU projector offload for any integrated GPU (`shared-memory-gpu`). On Apple Silicon (Metal), GPU memory is shared with the CPU but the projector loads fine — disabling offload there was unnecessary.

**Fix:** Skip the `shared-memory-gpu` disable for Metal GPUs, so projectors stay on the GPU there while remaining on CPU for other integrated GPUs (e.g. ROCm), as the tests define:

```go
if gpu.Integrated && gpu.DeviceID.Library != "Metal" {
    return true, "shared-memory-gpu"
}
```
